<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/1/barrier> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationNegative ;
    cav:judgement "-Agreements on additional quality checks, confidentiality requirements, and dissemination of the ECR data, are to beestablishedbetween theCommission and the MemberStates"@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeAlignmentBarrier ;
    m8g:hasRelatedService <http://example.org/analysis/interop/1> ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the alignment with existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/1/measure> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationPositive ;
    cav:judgement """This act ensures consistency and streamlines statistical processes in the area of European fisheries and aquaculture statistics.
Under the legal framework of Regulation (EC) No 223/2009.
Relying on data (Council Regulation (EC) No 1224/2009 of the European Parliament and of the Council and Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2017/218 of 6 February 2017),
Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2017/218.
Aligned with the DCF (Regulation (EU) No 2017/1004)."""@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeAlignmentMeasure ;
    m8g:hasRelatedService <http://example.org/analysis/interop/1> ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the alignment with existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/2/measure> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationPositive ;
    cav:judgement """-Asis the case forall European statistics disseminated by Eurostat,fisheries and aquaculture statistics are associated with ametadata description; - Member Statesare advisedto use the‘latest version of the SIMS’(see Commission Recommendation (EU) 2023/397). All tables disseminated by Eurostat are associated with ametadata description.
-Uses the existing network of statistical offices."""@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure ;
    m8g:hasRelatedService <http://example.org/analysis/interop/1> ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/3/barrier> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationNegative ;
    cav:judgement """-The specific data sources that the legislation aims to reuse may not use harmonised concepts andthegranularity of observations may hinder the reuse of data for the purpose of statistics;
-iplementation aspects may involve the creation of additional vocabularies."""@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeSharedBarrier ;
    m8g:hasRelatedService <http://example.org/analysis/interop/1> ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/3/measure> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationPositive ;
    cav:judgement """-Promotes the use of international standards for fisheries statistics, including concepts and classifications,such as the Fishing Areas for Statistical Purposes and the ASFISlist ofspecies.
-Promotes the alignment of the data requests, definitions, methodologies, and reporting formats with those oftheFAO and theOECD.
-Promotes the use of a clear definition for ‘aquaculture establishments’.
-Applies Regulation (EC) No1059/2003 of the European Parliament and of the Council to data on terrestrial units."""@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeSharedMeasure ;
    m8g:hasRelatedService <http://example.org/analysis/interop/1> ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/4/barrier> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationNegative ;
    cav:judgement "-Further developments are neededtoextract anddevelopthe data thatarecurrently stored in internal Commission repositories."@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeStandardsBarrier ;
    m8g:hasRelatedService <http://example.org/analysis/interop/1> ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standardsPlease list such measures"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/4/measure> a cav:Statement ;
    cav:interpretation iac:InterpretationPositive ;
    cav:judgement """-The data structure used in thisregulation should be comparable with the DCF set out in Regulation (EU) No2017/1004 of the European Parliament and of the Council.
-DG MARE collectsdata using the international FLUX standard (DG-MARE-FLUX-Brochure.pdf)."""@en ;
    cav:type iac:StatementTypeStandardsMeasure ;
    m8g:hasRelatedService <http://example.org/analysis/interop/1> ;
    dcterms:description "Assess the use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standardsPlease list such measures"@en .

<http://example.org/analysis/description/1> a iopa:BindingRequirement,
